version: "0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-09-27"
abstract: >-
  Standard-library Python research prototype. OES-32 scores a 32-channel block
  with S = 0.45·Peak + 0.35·RMS + 0.20·MeanAbs and latches at S ≥ τ (default
  τ = 0.50); OES-512 applies the same latch to 16 contiguous blocks of 32 to
  form a 16-bit coarse syndrome. Version 0.2.0 adds an optional, label-free
  self-calibrated τ (warm-up 99th percentile of block scores on robust-scaled
  residuals); the fixed default τ = 0.50 is retained. After the classical latch, an optional
  amplitude encoding maps the normalized vector to a 5-qubit (OES-32) or
  9-qubit (OES-512) feature state, with diagonal block projectors
  S_i = I − 2Π_i and Pauli-Z expectations for comparison. This is not a
  stabilizer QEC code, not a 32- or 512-qubit Hilbert space, and has not been
  run on quantum hardware. The normative residual contract is oes32-residual
  (ADR-001).
keywords:
  - oes512
  - oes32
  - residual
  - weighted latch
  - amplitude encoding
  - research prototype
